        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I'd like to link to a glossary definition of \"registrable domain\" <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42338\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42338/hovercard\">in the passkeys guide</a>. It turns out that although we don't have one, we do have a page for eTLD.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">But I think \"registrable domain\" is a better glossary entry, for three reasons:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>\"registrable domain\" is the <a href=\"https://url.spec.whatwg.org/#host-registrable-domain\" rel=\"nofollow\">spec term</a>. The spec doesn't talk about eTLD AFAICT.</li>\n<li>\"registrable domain\" is more comprehensible</li>\n<li>we never actually link to \"eTLD\" we only link to \"eTLD+1\", which is the same as registrable domain. So we currently have to link into a fragment of the glossary entry, rather than directly to it.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42588",
            "title": "Add glossary page for \"registrable domain\" instead of \"eTLD\"",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-01T00:42:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-31T19:31:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7963279?u=47d8ec0d8df2792d7f843e6f0db130da29b9308b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Flex-shrink example summary - more precision in explanation</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">After reading the section, it wasn't clear to me how it's calculated.<br>\nA reference for flex-grow explains it but it's not stated anywhere that flex-shrink uses the same mechanism.<br>\nWithout clearly stating it, it may be counter-intuitive as a paragraph above mentions that those calculations are more complicated than for flex-grow.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
