        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23125036?u=2652b638d8fde9fb96e59932ca59fc5be8f78cbd&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds anchors for all the fields in the <code class=\"notranslate\">chrome_settings_overrides</code> web extensions docs so they can be directly linked to.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I wanted to share a link to the <code class=\"notranslate\">search_provider</code> section but it is currently awkward to share a direct link to the right position as you can only use the \"Copy link to highlight\" version<a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Mozilla/Add-ons/WebExtensions/manifest.json/chrome_settings_overrides#search_url:~:text=Defines%20a%20search%20provider%20to%20add%20to%20the%20browser\" rel=\"nofollow\">0</a>, and even then it doesn't scroll as nicely as it does with an explicit anchor on the row imo.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/23125036/531559884-1a9242cd-e7a6-4ded-afa5-96f2b3469d60.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..HhaTfXeXVvH1SEAxISOJL6jn35Trk-e5ZeMyWkXutNw\"><img width=\"1260\" height=\"1451\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-01-02 at 8 49 51 pm\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/23125036/531559884-1a9242cd-e7a6-4ded-afa5-96f2b3469d60.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..HhaTfXeXVvH1SEAxISOJL6jn35Trk-e5ZeMyWkXutNw\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1451px;\"></a>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42580",
            "title": "Refactor `chrome_settings_overrides` page to use `<dl>` syntax",
            "date_modified": "2026-01-02T22:25:27.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-30T23:47:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "RobertCraigie",
                "url": "https://github.com/RobertCraigie"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/643434?u=f6a3c1d4e4f6c9f9b89180003bf3f1478fd6c5fa&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Current maxTouchPoints example is misleading IMHO</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I've checked the possible values of maxTouchPoints for different devices <a href=\"https://gist.github.com/tkrotoff/cd7ea4ec29f83111365772aaa21bb25b\">https://gist.github.com/tkrotoff/cd7ea4ec29f83111365772aaa21bb25b</a><br>\nand devices without touch screen (\"classic\" desktop computers) return 0</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42579",
            "title": "Improve maxTouchPoints example",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-31T03:26:04.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-30T23:31:58.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tkrotoff",
                "url": "https://github.com/tkrotoff"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184134219?u=2e3379684b8d674944164c3a6564fc3dd4c38f65&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Updated the glossary macro to point directly to \"Forbidden request header\" to resolve the build warning about the redirect.</p>\n\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42576",
            "title": "Fix glossary redirect warning",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-31T11:58:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-30T20:42:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Harish3005-cloud",
                "url": "https://github.com/Harish3005-cloud"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/184134219?u=2e3379684b8d674944164c3a6564fc3dd4c38f65&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Updated the syntax block to show that multiple preferences are allowed as per the RFC. Added an example demonstrating multiple preferences in a single header. <span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42535.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3763251282\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42535\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42535/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42535\">#42535</a></p>\n\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I updated the \"Syntax\" section to reflect that the <code class=\"notranslate\">Prefer</code> header accepts a comma-separated list of preferences. I also added a new \"Providing multiple preferences\" example to demonstrate this behavior.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">The RFC 7240 specification defines the <code class=\"notranslate\">Prefer</code> header grammar as <code class=\"notranslate\">1#preference</code>, meaning multiple preferences are allowed in a comma-separated list. The previous documentation implied only a single preference was valid, which was misleading for developers trying to set multiple directives (e.g., <code class=\"notranslate\">respond-async</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">wait</code>).</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Reference: <a href=\"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7240#section-2\" rel=\"nofollow\">RFC 7240 Section 2 - The Prefer Header Field</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42575",
            "title": "Fix(HTTP): Update Prefer header syntax to allow lists",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-30T18:57:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-30T18:56:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Harish3005-cloud",
                "url": "https://github.com/Harish3005-cloud"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">we reference keyframe selectors a bunch of times, but there was no reference page for them.</p>",
